                      00001 ;************************************************************************
                      00002 ;*      Microchip Technology Inc. 2002                                  *
                      00003 ;*      Assembler version: 2.0000                                       *
                      00004 ;*      Filename:                                                       *
                      00005 ;*              p16demo.asm (main routine)                              *
                      00006 ;*      Dependents:                                                     *
                      00007 ;*              p16lcd.asm                                              *
                      00008 ;*              p16math.asm                                             *
                      00009 ;*              16f877.lkr                                              *
                      00010 ;*      03/14/02                                                        *
                      00011 ;*      Designed to run at 4MHz                                         *
                      00012 ;*      PICDEM 2 PLUS DEMO code. The following functions are included   *
                      00013 ;*      with this code:                                                 *
                      00014 ;*              1. Voltmeter                                            *
                      00015 ;*                      The center tap of R16 is connected to RA0, the  *
                      00016 ;*                      A/D converter converts this analog voltage and  *
                      00017 ;*                      the result is displayed on the LCD in a range   *
                      00018 ;*                      from 0.00V - 5.00V.                             *
                      00019 ;*              2. Buzzer                                               *
                      00020 ;*                      The Piezo buzzer is connected to RC2 and is     *
                      00021 ;*                      driven by the CCP1 module. The period and duty  *
                      00022 ;*                      cycle are adjustable on the fly through the LCD *
                      00023 ;*                      and push-buttons.                               *
                      00024 ;*              3. Temperature                                          *
                      00025 ;*                      A TC74 Serial Digital Thermal Sensor is used to *
                      00026 ;*                      measure ambient temperature. The PIC and TC74   *
                      00027 ;*                      communicate using the MSSP module. The TC74 is  *
                      00028 ;*                      connected to the SDA & SCL I/O pins of the PIC  *
                      00029 ;*                      and functions as a slave. Every 2 seconds, the  *
                      00030 ;*                      temeperature is logged into the external EEPROM *
                      00031 ;*                      in a specific memory location.                  *
                      00032 ;*              4. Clock                                                *
                      00033 ;*                      This function is a real-time clock. When the    *
                      00034 ;*                      mode is entered, time begins at 00:00:00. The   *
                      00035 ;*                      user can set the time if desired.               *
                      00036 ;************************************************************************
                      00037 
                      00038 
                      00039 
